redstonepanel (1.13.2) noble; urgency=medium

  * Phantom LAN proxies for Bedrock servers, managed like add-ons (admins):
    Add-ons -> Server tools -> Phantom installs, starts, stops, restarts and
    uninstalls a Phantom (jhead/phantom 0.5.4, checked against a pinned
    SHA-256) that makes a server on a port other than 19132 show up under
    Friends -> LAN Games. It runs as phantom-<server>.service under the
    minecraft user, with a proxy port from 19300 up, and opens UDP 19132
    and that port in ufw. Install refuses while a Bedrock server holds
    19132, and explains why.
  * The tab also lists Phantom units made outside the panel that point at
    the server or hold its port, with their problems, Start / Stop and
    Remove unit (the unit file only). Removing a server removes its Phantom.

 -- Quentin Russell <quentin.russell@cielocloud.org>  Thu, 19 Nov 2026 23:59:00 +0000

redstonepanel (1.13.1) noble; urgency=medium

  * Java is installed when a server needs it, not with the package: Java
    moves from Recommends to Suggests, so Bedrock-only hosts get none.
    Creating, updating or restoring a Java server whose Java isn't
    installed offers to install the right openjdk-N-jre-headless (admins),
    then carries on. Servers that were waiting for it are moved onto it.
  * Dashboard -> Supporting services -> Java lists each installed Java with
    the servers on it, the ones servers need, and Install / Remove. Only a
    Java no server uses can be removed, and only when apt would remove
    nothing but that JRE.
  * Maintenance -> Java shows which Java a server runs on and switches it
    to another installed one that's new enough.
  * Update RedstonePanel from the dashboard (admins): Check for updates and
    Update now. The upgrade runs as its own systemd unit (redstonepanel
    upgrade, also usable from a terminal), so it survives the panel's
    restart; the page reloads on the new version. Game servers keep running.
  * Removing a server (Uninstall or Purge) closes its port in ufw and clears
    its failed state. The dashboard no longer lists failed units whose unit
    file is gone, such as servers removed by older versions, and clears them.
  * Browsers no longer keep running an old app.js after an update (a blank
    dashboard until Ctrl+F5): the panel's files are sent with
    Cache-Control: no-cache, and its pages link app.js and the stylesheet
    with the panel version.

 -- Quentin Russell <quentin.russell@cielocloud.org>  Thu, 19 Nov 2026 23:30:00 +0000

